# GRAPH RAG INTEGRATION [SHOULD]

**Fill / graph shape:** Rule **GRAPH.1** — `.cursor/rules/integrations/graph_rag_ingest.mdc` and `Cursor-Project/graph-rag/INGEST.md`. GRAPH.0 does **not** define how to populate Neo4j.

## Rule GRAPH.0: Auto-query Graph RAG for project questions

**Intent:** When the Graph RAG MCP server is available, Cursor agents SHOULD check the knowledge graph before answering Phoenix/project questions. Indexed layers (when filled) are the four GRAPH.1 zones: domain, API, test cases, Playwright.

**When to use `graph_query`:**
- Before answering Phoenix domain questions (business logic, endpoints, validations)
- When looking up API endpoints, DTOs, or enum values
- When checking test case coverage for a feature
- When looking for Playwright patterns or fixtures

**When NOT to use `graph_query`:**
- General programming questions unrelated to Phoenix
- Git/status operations
- Trivial Q&A, chit-chat
- When the user explicitly says to skip graph lookup

## Workflow [MUST after a successful `graph_query`]

Calling the graph is **SHOULD** when MCP is up. **Using** the result is **MUST**. Do not treat graph node text as wiki or as unopened Java rules.

1. **Wait for the graph.** Call `graph_query` with argument **`question`** (not `query`) and `use_llm_synthesis: false`. Do **not** Grep/Read the topic in the same turn as the first `graph_query`. After the tool returns, use **only** the **Open these sources** list (plus neighbors you opened from those paths).
2. **Open every `source_path` as live evidence:**
   - Phoenix `.java` / Swagger JSON → **Read** / Grep that file.
   - Confluence URL or `confluence_page_id` → **getConfluencePage**, then Rule 43 **REST fallback** (`get-confluence-page-rest.ps1 -PageId …`) if MCP 404s or is the wrong cloud. **Forbidden:** skipping the page and quoting the graph `description` as Confluence.
3. **Cite only what you opened.** Graph `description` / Qwen text is a pointer, not spec. If you did not open a wiki page, you MUST NOT write “Confluence says…” from the graph. If you did not open a Java file, you MUST NOT copy field rules (e.g. “required FK”) from a node.
4. **Counts from metadata only.** Node totals (`29`, `stale_count`) come from this turn’s `graph_status` / `graph_query` footer — not from memory or ingest comments.
5. **QA.0** on the files/pages you opened. Stale graph → **Ask before fill**, do not silently ingest.

## Available tools (GraphRAG MCP server)

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `graph_query` | Return `source_path` pointers (files + Confluence URLs). Argument name: **`question`**. Default: no LLM essay (`use_llm_synthesis: false`). |
| `graph_update` | Save verified facts **after user yes** (Ask before fill) |
| `graph_index_topic` | Index a specific topic across all sources on demand |
| `graph_status` | Show zone stats, node counts, system health |

## Ask before fill (user gate) [MUST]

The graph is filled **incrementally** (GRAPH.1). Agents MUST NOT call `graph_index_topic`, `graph_update`, or run ingest unless the user **agrees in this chat**.

**Ask** (pause until yes/no) when any of these is true:

1. **Graph empty** — `graph_status` total nodes is 0 (or MCP graph is down / returns no index).
2. **Empty for this question** — `graph_query` has no relevant hits, or only off-topic nodes (wrong topic’s `source_path` list). Do not treat another topic’s pointers as the answer.
3. **Stale** — `stale_count` > 0, or live file/wiki at `source_path` no longer matches the node (`source_hash` / content).
4. **Live mismatch** — after QA.0, code, Confluence, or Swagger disagrees with what graph nodes currently say.

The ask MUST name all three (no vague “should I update the graph?”):

| Field | Required content |
|-------|------------------|
| **What** | Topic and which nodes/edges would change (add / refresh / replace). |
| **From what** | Exact sources: Phoenix path + line range if known, Confluence title + page ID + URL, Swagger file + endpoint/DTO. |
| **What would be written** | GRAPH.1 node types and one-line facts to store (pointers + `source_path`). No placeholders, no whole-wiki dump, no four Swagger envs. |

Template:

```
Graph fill proposal
- What: …
- From what: …
- What would be written: …
May I apply this to the graph? (yes / no)
```

- **Yes** → scoped fill only (named topic ingest or verified `graph_update`). Parsers first (GRAPH.1). Then re-query.
- **No** → answer from live evidence only; leave Neo4j unchanged.
- Still answer the user’s Phoenix question from code/wiki even while waiting; do not block the Q&A on fill.

## After resolution

If live evidence produced **new verified** facts not in the graph, use the same **Ask before fill** template (do not silently `graph_update`). Chat nodes are enrichment, not a substitute for parsers (GRAPH.1).

## Graph visualization

Users can explore the knowledge graph visually at `http://localhost:7474` (Neo4j Browser) — spider-web view of all nodes, edges, and zones.

## Compliance tier

- **SHOULD** — Call `graph_query` when MCP is available (not a BLOCK if skipped).
- **MUST** — After a successful `graph_query`, open live `source_path`s (files + wiki REST on MCP fail). **Forbidden** to cite graph node text as Confluence or as unopened Java rules. Evidence gate (QA.0, 0.5) unchanged.
